# OpenEngine — Cursor rules (high-density IDE context)
# Read contracts/src/lib.rs (ARCH_VERSION) BEFORE writing code.

## Domain wall
- Domain B (crates/logic-sandbox, crates/math) is #![no_std] + forbid(unsafe_code). Pure FP only. Never add wgpu/winit/wasmtime/egui/rayon here.
- Domain A (crates/core, ecs, editor) may use std, wgpu, threads.
- All cross-domain data uses contracts types + postcard. Never invent ad-hoc messages.
- State flows ONE way: fn(&StateView) -> Result<WorldDelta, RecoverableError>.

## Determinism
- No raw f32 in logic. Use openengine-math I16F16 / fx!. No std::time, no scheduler dependence, no ambient randomness.

## Memory & SoA
- Always prefer bytemuck::cast_slice for SoA views. Never transmute.
- Never use Mutex in ECS hot paths; use atomic counters or lock-free queues (rayon is OK in Domain A).
- No Pod derive without #[repr(C)] and only POD fields.

## ABI
- All Wasm host functions must be defined in contracts/host_functions.rs (mirror spec). Don't scatter exports.
- Never reshape a #[repr(C)] struct or enum variant without bumping ARCH_VERSION + docs/abi/ + all consumers in one commit.

## Style
- deny(clippy::all). Fix, don't silence. Scoped #[allow] needs an inline reason.
- rustdoc for future cold agents: state invariants, lifetimes, safety preconditions.
